a('CHM-06','BIO-01','A suitable non-biopolymer copying network could provide a candidate replicating chemistry to test inside a proposed prebiotic protocell.','Replication in a chemical system would not establish a living protocell, compatible precursors, metabolism or open-ended evolution.','enabling')
a('BIO-04','BIO-01','A prebiotic chirality-selection mechanism could be investigated as one ingredient-selection step in a candidate protocell experiment.','Homochirality is not asserted necessary for every possible protocell, and would not establish replication or life.')
a('BIO-05','GEN-02','Functional assignments could provide test cases and constraints for a candidate regulatory grammar.','Annotation is not a predictive grammar, and function can depend on cellular context.')
a('BIO-07','BME-01','A tissue-growth controller could supply candidate size and growth-termination conditions for a regeneration intervention.','Cell-size control does not establish vascularization, scarlessness or functional organ replacement.','enabling')
a('BCH-05','LON-08','A sequence-to-condensate model could help test whether a specified assembly/disassembly process contributes to a proteostasis problem.','No particular condensate is assumed causal in aging, and predicting phase behavior does not establish a therapy.')
a('BCH-06','BCH-10','A qualified coupling mechanism could inform the energy-conversion component of a candidate biochemical network.','Modern membrane machinery may violate a particular minimal/prebiotic design, and an energy module does not establish autonomy.','enabling')
a('BCH-07','BIF-08','Modification-response rules could constrain the post-translational context used when testing a broader cellular regulation model.','Post-translational and post-transcriptional regulation are distinct; this is contextual coupling, not decoding one code from the other.')
a('BCH-08','BIF-06','Membrane insertion and topology rules could provide candidate structural constraints for membrane-protein interaction models.','Topology does not determine binding pose or affinity and does not cover every protein family.','enabling')
a('BCH-09','BCH-01','An identified quantum contribution could supply a mechanism to include or reject in a selected enzyme-catalysis model.','No universal biological quantum effect is assumed; a restricted mechanism would not establish a full catalytic theory.')
a('BIF-05','GEN-06','Resolved haplotypes could improve the sequence representation used for proposed epistasis comparisons.','Assembly does not identify interaction effects, and a perfect universal assembler is not necessary for particular experiments.')
a('GEN-06','GEN-09','Interaction maps could supply candidate gene-pair hypotheses for tests of intrinsic incompatibility.','Epistasis alone does not establish sterility, lineage-wide rules or the cause of reproductive isolation.','enabling')
a('GEN-08','BIF-03','A dosage-compensation model could provide a chromosome-scale regulation case for a dynamics predictor.','Sex-chromosome silencing does not determine every regulatory interaction or cell context.','enabling')
a('GEN-05','GEN-10','Mechanistic examples of new-gene integration could help test hypotheses about novelty and mutational robustness.','A catalog of gene functions does not establish universal evolvability laws.')
a('GEN-10','AGR-10','A qualified robustness model could help compare candidate trait modifications in a domestication design.','It would not establish immediate domestication, field fitness or the usefulness of a new staple.')
a('BIF-07','MIC-02','Strain/function estimates could provide community-state observations against which to test an assembly model.','A profiler does not establish causal ecological interactions or predict stability.','enabling')
a('BIF-09','BIF-04','An atlas-query interface could provide an inspectable way for a proposed bioinformatics scientist to retrieve and compare datasets.','Interactive access does not establish zero latency, sound inference or scientific autonomy.')
a('BOT-02','AGR-04','Systemic-signal models could motivate candidate plant-defense activation experiments.','No signal is assumed to provide cost-free resistance to every pest or pathogen.','enabling')
a('BOT-05','BOT-04','If confirmed, a microtubule sensing mechanism could supply one component of the wall/growth feedback model.','The hypothesis has not been confirmed here, and it would not resolve the complete regulatory network.','enabling')
a('BOT-04','BIO-07','A plant wall/growth feedback model could provide a mechanistic plant-cell case for testing size and tissue-scaling control.','A plant-cell mechanism cannot be generalized to all cells or organs by assumption.','enabling')
a('BOT-10','BIO-07','Division-plane rules could provide geometric constraints in a model of tissue growth and organization.','Division geometry does not determine growth rate, adult size or every tissue’s scaling.','enabling')
a('BOT-06','AGR-06','A heritable stress-response mechanism could be tested as one route to retaining a selected tolerance trait across generations.','It would not establish tolerance to every climate stress, commercial yield or no fitness trade-off.','enabling')
a('BOT-06','AGR-04','A stable epigenetic response could be investigated as one non-sequence-change route to a selected defensive trait.','Non-GM status, durability and resistance coverage require separate evaluation; no universal defense is established.')
a('BOT-04','AGR-08','Cell-wall and growth models could help compare candidate root architectures in a carbon-allocation design.','Root architecture does not establish stable soil storage or the source’s carbon-per-hectare and yield targets.')
a('AGR-03','AGR-08','A qualified photosynthetic pathway could change the carbon-input assumptions in a proposed crop carbon budget.','Additional fixed carbon can go to harvest or respiration; stable soil sequestration and no yield penalty do not follow.')
a('ZOO-02','ROB-05','Explicit local interaction rules could supply candidate policies for testing robot coordination without a leader.','Animal alignment does not establish heterogeneous robot reliability, communication tolerance or instantaneous behavior.','enabling')
a('ZOO-05','NEU-04','A qualified vertebrate patterning circuit could motivate candidate regulators to test in a specified neural-repair context.','Cross-species transfer, brain function and safe adult regeneration remain unestablished.')
