a('MIC-10','IMM-04','Metabolite/receptor hypotheses could provide a molecular representation to test within a tissue-specific immune-interaction model.','Host phenotypes are not all immune responses, and molecular mapping does not establish complete causal behavior across body sites.','enabling')
a('VIR-03','CLM-03','A qualified persistence-state intervention could provide one route for testing control of a specified viral reservoir.','A latency switch does not itself establish safe reservoir eradication or a durable cure for all persistent infections.','enabling')
a('VIR-04','VIR-09','A host-adaptation model could help state selection criteria and safety constraints for a defined attenuation experiment.','A spillover model does not produce desired traits or predict safe clinical behavior.')
a('VIR-09','VIR-04','Controlled experimental trajectories could provide limited tests of an adaptation model.','Laboratory selection does not recreate real-world spillover ecology; this is feedback, not circular validation.','feedback')
a('VIR-07','CLM-07','A qualified viral vector could be a delivery option for a specified in-vivo editing intervention.','Viral and non-viral routes are alternatives in design space; neither establishes any-disease editing, safety or lifelong benefit.','enabling')
a('VIR-07','ONC-02','A targeted oncolytic implementation could be investigated as one intervention component in a metastatic-tumor program.','Payload delivery does not establish clearance of all metastatic cells or universal safety.','enabling')
a('IMM-03','IMM-05','A trained-memory model could help formulate tests of persistent immune responses to defined environmental exposures.','Innate memory is not assumed to explain all allergy or autoimmunity patterns.')
a('IMM-06','IMM-02','A qualified response predictor could help compare proposed antigen designs across specified host histories.','A prediction is not sterilizing lifelong immunity or proof of coverage of all mutable strains.')
a('NEU-09','HCI-01','An encoding/decoding model could inform the interpretation layer of a proposed bidirectional neural interface.','It would not supply non-invasive single-neuron sensors, safe writing or perfect fidelity.','enabling')
a('NEU-09','NEU-03','A coding model could help state testable hypotheses about stored and retrieved neural representations.','General coding rules do not establish long-term engram storage or a complete memory mechanism.')
a('NEU-03','HCI-10','A qualified retrieval model could inform a design linking external records to selected recall cues.','It would not establish direct memory writing, seamless cognition or the effectiveness of augmentation.')
a('NEU-03','NEU-05','A storage/retrieval model could provide defined memory outcomes for testing proposed sleep-related mechanisms.','This does not establish why sleep is necessary or what dreams do.')
a('NEU-05','NEU-03','A specified sleep-state mechanism could provide perturbation hypotheses for testing memory stabilization.','This is proposed experimental feedback; neither full theory is proven by the other.','feedback')
a('NEU-02','HCI-08','A perceptual-binding model could help define tests of visual, spatial and contextual cue consistency in a shared environment.','A model of binding does not create the display channels or guarantee physical co-location.')
a('NEU-10','MLC-10','A specified neural dynamical rule could motivate a computational mechanism to test in a cognitive architecture.','Biological descriptions need not transfer to an effective algorithm, and no rule or AGI performance is established here.')
a('LON-04','LON-01','Identified circulating factors could be candidates to test as one intervention component in a systemic-aging program.','Animal or blood-factor effects would not establish safe, complete systemic human rejuvenation.','enabling')
